/**
\class pdg::Scene
\ingroup Animation
\brief Own layers, an isolated physics world, camera advancement and logical timers.

Scenes draw in construction order above legacy layers. pause() freezes simulation,
physics, owned camera animation and timers while rendering continues. A later HUD
scene can share the same Port and continue advancing. Layer camera overrides remain
supported; a camera has only one automatic scene owner.

removeLayer() transfers responsibility without destruction. disposeLayer() destroys
an attached layer. dispose() cancels timers, disconnects subscribe() registrations,
destroys attached layers and releases the world; detached layers survive. Disposal
is idempotent and physical cleanup is deferred during traversal. Detach and attach
outside traversal and disconnect cross-layer constraints before detachment.

setFixedStep(), advance(), getSimulationTime() and getDroppedTime() use seconds;
timer creation and delays use milliseconds. Fixed step zero selects variable-step
updates. Host admission is limited to 0.25 seconds and eight fixed steps per update.
Discarded time does not advance timers. Fixed-step interpolation affects sprite
root transforms during rendering; physics and queries use authoritative state.
Camera and skeletal poses hold current state. Timer IDs are positive and local.
Repeating intervals must be positive and fire at most once per step. Scene resume
preserves individual timer pauses and excludes elapsed paused time. setTimeScale()
accepts finite nonnegative values; zero freezes advancement without explicit pause.

subscribe(emitter, handler, type) retains the handler and disconnects the exact
registration on disposal; the emitter may be destroyed first. cancel/unsubscribe
operations on unknown IDs do nothing. Raw input is controlled independently with
setInputEnabled(). Audio and external asynchronous work remain application policy.

\note Include pdg/sys/scene.h, pdg/sys/spritelayer.h and pdg/sys/sprite.h. Native stack scenes are
supported. Heap scenes use addRef()/release() following PDG conventions. Explicitly
dispose() before abandoning a scene. Shared ports and artwork retain existing ownership.

\code{.cpp}
pdg::Scene gameplay, hud;
gameplay.setManual(true);
hud.setManual(true);
gameplay.setFixedStep(1.0 / 60);
auto* actors = gameplay.createSpriteLayer();
auto* indicator = hud.createSpriteLayer()->createSprite();
indicator->setSpin(2);
gameplay.pause();
gameplay.advance(0.1); // Held pose.
hud.advance(0.1);      // Independent HUD animation.
gameplay.resume();
gameplay.removeLayer(actors);
hud.addLayer(actors);  // Explicitly transfer the surviving layer.
hud.disposeLayer(actors);
\endcode
*/
